# object-storage

The object-storage gateway: a codefly/storage/v0 gRPC service backed by MinIO locally and a cloud object store when deployed.

Local data survives container replacement in the agent's Codefly home. A new
store initializes on its first run when its custody directory is absent or
empty; a directory holding data without a custody record fails closed.
Existing anonymous-volume stores require explicit recovery;
see https://github.com/codefly-dev/service-object-storage/blob/main/docs/local-minio-recovery.md.

Presigned URLs are signed for `presign-host` (service.codefly.yaml, or
`SOS_PRESIGN_HOST`) on the published MinIO port. The gateway itself dials MinIO
as host.docker.internal. A local run without `presign-host` is refused.
